{"route":"/docs/4.0/layout/overview/","version":"4.0","renderedVersion":"4.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Overview","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Components and options for laying out your Bootstrap project, including wrapping containers, a powerful grid system, a flexible media object, and responsive utility classes."},"blocks":[{"id":"containers","type":"heading","en":"Containers","level":2},{"id":"containers--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Containers are the most basic layout element in Bootstrap and are <strong>required when using our default grid system</strong>. Choose from a responsive, fixed-width container (meaning its <code>max-width</code> changes at each breakpoint) or fluid-width (meaning it’s <code>100%</code> wide all the time)."},{"id":"containers--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"While containers <em>can</em> be nested, most layouts do not require a nested container."},{"id":"containers--example-1","type":"demo","key":"7e584610c7016054b906","height":147},{"id":"containers--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"container\">\n  <!-- Content here -->\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"containers--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Use <code>.container-fluid</code> for a full width container, spanning the entire width of the viewport."},{"id":"containers--example-2","type":"demo","key":"14001296a0fceebb3ce3","height":147},{"id":"containers--code-2","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"container-fluid\">\n  ...\n</div>","language":"html"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints","type":"heading","en":"Responsive breakpoints","level":2},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Since Bootstrap is developed to be mobile first, we use a handful of <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Media_Queries/Using_media_queries\">media queries</a> to create sensible breakpoints for our layouts and interfaces. These breakpoints are mostly based on minimum viewport widths and allow us to scale up elements as the viewport changes."},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap primarily uses the following media query ranges—or breakpoints—in our source Sass files for our layout, grid system, and components."},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--code-1","type":"code","value":"// Extra small devices (portrait phones, less than 576px)\n// No media query since this is the default in Bootstrap\n\n// Small devices (landscape phones, 576px and up)\n@media (min-width: 576px) { ... }\n\n// Medium devices (tablets, 768px and up)\n@media (min-width: 768px) { ... }\n\n// Large devices (desktops, 992px and up)\n@media (min-width: 992px) { ... }\n\n// Extra large devices (large desktops, 1200px and up)\n@media (min-width: 1200px) { ... }","language":"scss"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Since we write our source CSS in Sass, all our media queries are available via Sass mixins:"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--code-2","type":"code","value":"@include media-breakpoint-up(xs) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-up(sm) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-up(md) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-up(lg) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-up(xl) { ... }\n\n// Example usage:\n@include media-breakpoint-up(sm) {\n  .some-class {\n    display: block;\n  }\n}","language":"scss"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"We occasionally use media queries that go in the other direction (the given screen size <em>or smaller</em>):"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--code-3","type":"code","value":"// Extra small devices (portrait phones, less than 576px)\n@media (max-width: 575.98px) { ... }\n\n// Small devices (landscape phones, less than 768px)\n@media (max-width: 767.98px) { ... }\n\n// Medium devices (tablets, less than 992px)\n@media (max-width: 991.98px) { ... }\n\n// Large devices (desktops, less than 1200px)\n@media (max-width: 1199.98px) { ... }\n\n// Extra large devices (large desktops)\n// No media query since the extra-large breakpoint has no upper bound on its width","language":"scss"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"Note that since browsers do not currently support <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/mediaqueries-4/#range-context\">range context queries</a>, we work around the limitations of <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/mediaqueries-4/#mq-min-max\"><code>min-</code> and <code>max-</code> prefixes</a> and viewports with fractional widths (which can occur under certain conditions on high-dpi devices, for instance) by using values with higher precision for these comparisons."}]},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"Once again, these media queries are also available via Sass mixins:"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--code-4","type":"code","value":"@include media-breakpoint-down(xs) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-down(sm) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-down(md) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-down(lg) { ... }","language":"scss"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"There are also media queries and mixins for targeting a single segment of screen sizes using the minimum and maximum breakpoint widths."},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--code-5","type":"code","value":"// Extra small devices (portrait phones, less than 576px)\n@media (max-width: 575.98px) { ... }\n\n// Small devices (landscape phones, 576px and up)\n@media (min-width: 576px) and (max-width: 767.98px) { ... }\n\n// Medium devices (tablets, 768px and up)\n@media (min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 991.98px) { ... }\n\n// Large devices (desktops, 992px and up)\n@media (min-width: 992px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) { ... }\n\n// Extra large devices (large desktops, 1200px and up)\n@media (min-width: 1200px) { ... }","language":"scss"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"These media queries are also available via Sass mixins:"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--code-6","type":"code","value":"@include media-breakpoint-only(xs) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-only(sm) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-only(md) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-only(lg) { ... }\n@include media-breakpoint-only(xl) { ... }","language":"scss"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"Similarly, media queries may span multiple breakpoint widths:"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--code-7","type":"code","value":"// Example\n// Apply styles starting from medium devices and up to extra large devices\n@media (min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) { ... }","language":"scss"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"The Sass mixin for targeting the same screen size range would be:"},{"id":"responsive-breakpoints--code-8","type":"code","value":"@include media-breakpoint-between(md, xl) { ... }","language":"scss"},{"id":"z-index","type":"heading","en":"Z-index","level":2},{"id":"z-index--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Several Bootstrap components utilize <code>z-index</code>, the CSS property that helps control layout by providing a third axis to arrange content. We utilize a default z-index scale in Bootstrap that’s been designed to properly layer navigation, tooltips and popovers, modals, and more."},{"id":"z-index--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"These higher values start at an arbitrary number, high and specific enough to ideally avoid conflicts. We need a standard set of these across our layered components—tooltips, popovers, navbars, dropdowns, modals—so we can be reasonably consistent in the behaviors. There’s no reason we couldn’t have used <code>100</code>+ or <code>500</code>+."},{"id":"z-index--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"We don’t encourage customization of these individual values; should you change one, you likely need to change them all."},{"id":"z-index--code-1","type":"code","value":"$zindex-dropdown:          1000 !default;\n$zindex-sticky:            1020 !default;\n$zindex-fixed:             1030 !default;\n$zindex-modal-backdrop:    1040 !default;\n$zindex-modal:             1050 !default;\n$zindex-popover:           1060 !default;\n$zindex-tooltip:           1070 !default;","language":"scss"},{"id":"z-index--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"To handle overlapping borders within components (e.g., buttons and inputs in input groups), we use low single digit <code>z-index</code> values of <code>1</code>, <code>2</code>, and <code>3</code> for default, hover, and active states. On hover/focus/active, we bring a particular element to the forefront with a higher <code>z-index</code> value to show their border over the sibling elements."}],"demos":[{"key":"7e584610c7016054b906","html":"\n  <div class=\"bd-example-container\">\n    <div class=\"bd-example-container-header\"></div>\n    <div class=\"bd-example-container-sidebar\"></div>\n    <div class=\"bd-example-container-body\"></div>\n  </div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"14001296a0fceebb3ce3","html":"\n  <div class=\"bd-example-container bd-example-container-fluid\">\n    <div class=\"bd-example-container-header\"></div>\n    <div class=\"bd-example-container-sidebar\"></div>\n    <div class=\"bd-example-container-body\"></div>\n  </div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Getting started","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/download/"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/contents/"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/browsers-devices/"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/g